{"schemaVersion":1,"storyId":"the-bottle-garden","version":1,"title":"The Bottle Garden","ageTiers":["5-6","7-8"],"language":"en","narrationLocale":"en-GH","pages":[{"n":1,"text":"Shamsia and her brother Mubarak walked home from school. By the road, there were empty plastic bottles everywhere. ‘That is a lot of rubbish,’ said Shamsia.","sentences":["Shamsia and her brother Mubarak walked home from school.","By the road, there were empty plastic bottles everywhere.","‘That is a lot of rubbish,’ said Shamsia."],"alt":"Two children walk past a roadside with many plastic bottles lying about.","image":{"hash":"sha256:fe59a8782a49c7d01393ede51f352be05608a69ffe877da3b0149612ec3af366","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:643631ca64edfde660006f52141aab0af66f428cb7fbcd799516207efbc67ce6","durationMs":15760,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,5783],[5783,11751],[11751,15760]],"words":[[0,806],[806,1152],[1152,1498],[1498,2304],[2304,3111],[3111,3802],[3802,4263],[4263,4723],[4723,5783],[5783,6014],[6014,6359],[6359,7004],[7004,7580],[7580,8041],[8041,8617],[8617,9424],[9424,10230],[10230,11751],[11751,12212],[12212,12442],[12442,12557],[12557,12903],[12903,13133],[13133,14124],[14124,14585],[14585,15760]]}}},{"n":2,"text":"‘Plastic does not rot away fast,’ she said. ‘It stays for a very long time. We should not throw it on the ground.’ ‘Can we use it again?’ asked Mubarak.","sentences":["‘Plastic does not rot away fast,’ she said.","‘It stays for a very long time.","We should not throw it on the ground.’ ‘Can we use it again?’ asked Mubarak."],"alt":"A girl and her brother look at a bottle in the grass.","image":{"hash":"sha256:ce1d589942e41430ffce849ae41f58dc706a258e0b9eb88524cab704eb544b80","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:875b7e6a356691f6e4ebdf075b7d57bc10ed1d99207164fe33d960a14d071237","durationMs":12320,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,3525],[3525,6035],[6035,12320]],"words":[[0,671],[671,1054],[1054,1341],[1341,1629],[1629,2012],[2012,2548],[2548,2836],[2836,3525],[3525,3717],[3717,4196],[4196,4483],[4483,4579],[4579,4962],[4962,5346],[5346,6035],[6035,6227],[6227,6802],[6802,7089],[7089,7568],[7568,7760],[7760,7951],[7951,8239],[8239,9120],[9120,9408],[9408,9599],[9599,9887],[9887,10078],[10078,10864],[10864,11343],[11343,12320]]}}},{"n":3,"text":"At home, Uncle Acheampong smiled. ‘Yes,’ he said. ‘We can reuse clean bottles. Let us make a bottle garden.’ He found five clean empty bottles from the house.","sentences":["At home, Uncle Acheampong smiled.","‘Yes,’ he said.","‘We can reuse clean bottles.","Let us make a bottle garden.’ He found five clean empty bottles from the house."],"alt":"An uncle holds up five clean empty bottles in the yard.","image":{"hash":"sha256:2869d0440074e13c465df7746ea0f9885ee27c97a2aec2247014fa1c374b7ee2","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:eb634fc39e658c1a64db5fc04f4744e4fb6f92869638768b320ac8a005767bdd","durationMs":16680,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,3811],[3811,5464],[5464,8484],[8484,16680]],"words":[[0,240],[240,911],[911,1510],[1510,2708],[2708,3811],[3811,4362],[4362,4601],[4601,5464],[5464,5704],[5704,6063],[6063,6662],[6662,7262],[7262,8484],[8484,8843],[8843,9083],[9083,9562],[9562,9682],[9682,10401],[10401,11503],[11503,11743],[11743,12342],[12342,12822],[12822,13421],[13421,14020],[14020,14859],[14859,15338],[15338,15697],[15697,16680]]}}},{"n":4,"text":"Uncle Acheampong cut a long window in the side of each bottle. He made small holes in the bottom for water to drain. ‘Children must not use scissors alone,’ he said. ‘Ask a grown-up.’","sentences":["Uncle Acheampong cut a long window in the side of each bottle.","He made small holes in the bottom for water to drain.","‘Children must not use scissors alone,’ he said.","‘Ask a grown-up.’"],"alt":"An uncle cuts a bottle with scissors while the children watch from a safe distance.","image":{"hash":"sha256:a7f0f9497894b6bbd12e19bb4fffc93a2f437e62d8009accae27bed55edd2fe6","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:2637f6607534cc99baf2ee3d4d21188a49c61f429dd0d6be56b17fcf8e9f1fb4","durationMs":15880,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,5472],[5472,10120],[10120,14420],[14420,15880]],"words":[[0,514],[514,1543],[1543,1851],[1851,1954],[1954,2366],[2366,2983],[2983,3188],[3188,3497],[3497,3908],[3908,4114],[4114,4525],[4525,5472],[5472,5677],[5677,6089],[6089,6603],[6603,7117],[7117,7323],[7323,7631],[7631,8249],[8249,8557],[8557,9071],[9071,9277],[9277,10120],[10120,10943],[10943,11355],[11355,11663],[11663,11972],[11972,12795],[12795,13473],[13473,13679],[13679,14420],[14420,14728],[14728,14831],[14831,15880]]}}},{"n":5,"text":"Shamsia and Mubarak filled each bottle with soil. They pushed in seeds. ‘One, two, three, four, five bottles,’ counted Mubarak. They gave each seed a little water.","sentences":["Shamsia and Mubarak filled each bottle with soil.","They pushed in seeds.","‘One, two, three, four, five bottles,’ counted Mubarak.","They gave each seed a little water."],"alt":"Children fill bottles with soil and plant seeds while counting.","image":{"hash":"sha256:2bc06edb2ec0653c75cda30f74a1bed17f45d35a70f825cc7c60e6ece9436ce6","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:9b9316e21dbdfd8e07c7e239b5430f6865209b48305231efa754a41ecd637074","durationMs":19920,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,5998],[5998,8739],[8739,15686],[15686,19920]],"words":[[0,950],[950,1357],[1357,2307],[2307,3121],[3121,3664],[3664,4478],[4478,5021],[5021,5998],[5998,6540],[6540,7355],[7355,7626],[7626,8739],[8739,9363],[9363,9987],[9987,10883],[10883,11643],[11643,12185],[12185,13352],[13352,14302],[14302,15686],[15686,16229],[16229,16772],[16772,17315],[17315,17857],[17857,17993],[17993,18807],[18807,19920]]}}},{"n":6,"text":"Uncle Acheampong tied each bottle to the fence with string. Now the garden hung in the sun, a row of little green pots. ‘It looks like a green necklace!’ said Shamsia.","sentences":["Uncle Acheampong tied each bottle to the fence with string.","Now the garden hung in the sun, a row of little green pots.","‘It looks like a green necklace!’ said Shamsia."],"alt":"Five bottles tied to a fence by string, with small seedlings in each.","image":{"hash":"sha256:b57a668a670d660cf597c7908c15e45373a2003ebc426f88965cde9cef384fa3","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:4335218cf774fc17b274cb999c00e9fccf5023b40f4764f421cd86916b92cca8","durationMs":15440,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,5581],[5581,10906],[10906,15440]],"words":[[0,535],[535,1604],[1604,2032],[2032,2459],[2459,3101],[3101,3315],[3315,3635],[3635,4170],[4170,4598],[4598,5581],[5581,5902],[5902,6223],[6223,6865],[6865,7292],[7292,7506],[7506,7827],[7827,8319],[8319,8426],[8426,8746],[8746,8960],[8960,9602],[9602,10137],[10137,10906],[10906,11120],[11120,11655],[11655,12083],[12083,12189],[12189,12724],[12724,13922],[13922,14349],[14349,15440]]}}},{"n":7,"text":"Every day, they gave their bottle garden a drink. Soon, tiny green shoots peeped out. ‘We made a garden from rubbish!’ said Mubarak.","sentences":["Every day, they gave their bottle garden a drink.","Soon, tiny green shoots peeped out.","‘We made a garden from rubbish!’ said Mubarak."],"alt":"Two children water hanging bottles with tiny green shoots.","image":{"hash":"sha256:ef3f7d2b3fc771e015b36298abedd433f54be6508103ab9d76b97f9d49b7fb96","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:704f17ed6c57d9c1b844a8bb71e7a0707ddc65e8aceeb1b10bea81aba4c01da9","durationMs":13880,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,5152],[5152,9010],[9010,13880]],"words":[[0,588],[588,1129],[1129,1600],[1600,2070],[2070,2658],[2658,3364],[3364,4070],[4070,4188],[4188,5152],[5152,5811],[5811,6281],[6281,6869],[6869,7575],[7575,8281],[8281,9010],[9010,9245],[9245,9716],[9716,9834],[9834,10539],[10539,11010],[11010,12210],[12210,12680],[12680,13880]]}}},{"n":8,"text":"From then on, Shamsia put her empty bottles in the bin. ‘Reuse it or bin it,’ she said. ‘Never throw it on the ground.’ The end.","sentences":["From then on, Shamsia put her empty bottles in the bin.","‘Reuse it or bin it,’ she said.","‘Never throw it on the ground.’ The end."],"alt":"A girl drops a bottle into a bin beside the road.","image":{"hash":"sha256:d70f8e449fb355c7b74f1b731b6ed1fee75619a3fb065068c9a9630eaaca840c","width":960,"height":717},"audio":{"hash":"sha256:e6ebb462f8b77486cfa77adba9395ec86d269ba6b45b646836d19b6f16dfb470","durationMs":12560,"timing":{"granularity":"word","method":"tts-marks","verified":true,"sentences":[[0,5508],[5508,8481],[8481,12560]],"words":[[0,461],[461,922],[922,1337],[1337,2143],[2143,2489],[2489,2835],[2835,3411],[3411,4217],[4217,4448],[4448,4794],[4794,5508],[5508,6084],[6084,6315],[6315,6545],[6545,6891],[6891,7306],[7306,7651],[7651,8481],[8481,9057],[9057,9633],[9633,9864],[9864,10094],[10094,10440],[10440,11500],[11500,11846],[11846,12560]]}}}],"activities":[{"id":"bottle-c1","type":"comprehension","afterPage":3,"question":"Who cut the bottles?","options":["Uncle Acheampong","Mubarak","Shamsia"],"correctIndex":0},{"id":"bottle-c2","type":"comprehension","afterPage":5,"question":"How many bottles did they use?","options":["Five","Ten","Two"],"correctIndex":0},{"id":"bottle-ph","type":"phonics","afterPage":6,"targetSound":"b","prompt":"Which words start with the b sound, like bottle?","options":["bottle","bin","seed","brother"],"correctIndexes":[0,1,3]},{"id":"bottle-s1","type":"sequencing","prompt":"Put the story in order.","items":["The children see bottles by the road.","Uncle Acheampong cuts the bottles.","The children plant seeds.","The bottle garden grows."]},{"id":"bottle-sel","type":"sel","afterPage":8,"prompt":"The children turn